   "sentenceId": 24,
   "he": "וְהַשּׁוֹתֶה מַיִם לִצְמָאוֹ וְכוּ׳: לְאַפּוֹקֵי מַאי? אֲמַר רַב אִידֵּי בַּר אָבִין: לְאַפּוֹקֵי לְמַאן",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna that the tanna’im disagreed with regard to one who «drinks water» to quench «his thirst.» The Gemara asks: «What does» this emphasis on his thirst come «to exclude? Rav Idi bar Avin said:» It comes «to exclude one»"
  },
  {
   "id": "berakhot.45a.1",
   "daf": "45a",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "דַּחֲנַקְתֵּיהּ אוּמְצָא.",
   "en": "«who was choked by a piece of meat» and drank water in order to wash it down. He need not recite a blessing."
  }
 ],
